{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod","id":788708,"title":"Hunter: the Reckoning vs Vigil-type hunters in the oWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-18T06:19:19-08:00","id":788708,"title":"Hunter: the Reckoning vs Vigil-type hunters in the oWoD","content":"I know that everyone is interested in the CoD, and that oWoD is not really subject to revisions (beyond minor flourishes that can be squeezed into a 20th Anniversary edition), but there is one aspect of the oWoD I feel needs a retouch: Hunters. Where to start? I love CoD's Hunter: the Vigil, and feel that there are elements of oWoD hunter organizations that could fit Vigil-style in an oWoD compilation of monster hunters.<br /> <br /> I feel that Vigil got everything right both in storyteller and a mechanics level. From the different tiers to the ways in which mortals get involved in monster hunting to the Endowments of the different conspiracies and how they get them. Everything, just everything felt right, made sense, and fit. Hunter: the Reckoning, on the other hand was the exact opposite. Everything about Imbued hunters felt awkward and clunky both from a storytelling perspective to a game mechanics perspective. The Heralds were too much of a Deus Ex Machina, some of the hunter splats didn't make sense (Innocents anyone?), the Edges were nerfed compared to the monsters that you hunted, the heirarchy of the Edges didn't make sense, and the way that you gained Conviction by gambling Conviction, particularly to go up in Virtue....it just didn't work. Add to that a lack of folklore concerning Imbued hunters and it just seemed out of place.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are already Vigil-like elements in the oWoD that could be used to make an anniversary book on oWoD monster hunters. Demon Hunter X gives us the Shih and the Technocracy-controlled Strike Force Zero, The Inquisition gives us the Society of Leopold and drops hints of other hunter organizations around the world that use Faith and/or Theurgy as their weapons, and there is even an Exorcist book detailing Demon (the Fallen) hunters. The Technocracy even plies its hand at monster hunting from time to time. I think there is enough material here to compile a comprehensive volume of monster hunters in the oWoD. One that may or may not leave out the Imbued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T07:37:25-08:00","id":788740,"title":"","content":"Yes, the last paragraph is on point. &quot;Vigil-style&quot; is what we would have originally called &quot;The Hunter's Hunted&quot;. Reckoning is a very different game, meant to suddenly fling normal people who had been unquestioning of their lives into the deep end to see if they would sink or swim in a world full of monsters hiding their existences from public knowledge. Think <i>They Live</i>, but with an effect that can't be stolen or broken like the sunglasses, and instead of aliens, you're seeing shadows, and possibly even more weird details if you have the edges to differentiate between monsters.<br /> <br /> Edit: And the powers are kind of like the ones that Contractors would get in the closer to contemporary (and very much after the endgame runs for the lines) <i>Darker Than Black</i>. Usually, however, the triggers aren't quite as onerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-18-2015, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T10:27:39-08:00","id":788849,"title":"","content":"cWOD non-Imbued hunters already got an X20 book: Hunters Hunted II (though it doesn't cover all of them).<br /> <br /> On top of almost all the existing source material on them.<br /> <br /> Reckoning has made in the context of needing something that wasn't HH or HtV to bother making a full book about them. Otherwise HtR would have just been a collection of hunters from earlier books; not a full game line on its own.<br /> <br /> I've also run plenty of HtR, and I think your analysis of it is a bit biased. I'm not saying it's a game for you, if HtV is your deal, and the cWOD hunter groups that fit more into its style are what you want, game on. But the Heralds aren't really Deus ex Machina once you get into the lore of the game, some of the Creeds are hard to grok but none of them fail to make sense (if you want a perfect example of an Innocent in pop culture, Xander from Buffy the Vampire Slayer is one of my top choices), the Edges are what they are as HtR expects you to use its present monster creation rules to customize what you need (just like HtV does) rather than use the other cWOD supernaturals and you're supposed to be weaker than monsters so either lucky or smarts are your best weapons, and you can get Conviction in ways other than gambling.<br /> <br /> All in all, it sounds far more like you didn't really get into HtR's conceptual goal. Which is, again, fine, as it isn't something you have to get into. But a lot of what you're saying are bugs, are in fact features from the prospective of what the game is trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T14:15:54-08:00","id":788958,"title":"","content":"For more like an organized organized than hunters hunted but more crossover friendly than hunter the reckoning I'd actually recommend the sorcerer books(albeit with heavy house ruling, but in a crossover that's expected.)<br /> <br /> Sorcerer paths work surprisingly well if you play them more toward Geralt of Rivia than Harry potter, especially if you cross them with the other numina available to humans through the different game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T20:03:14-08:00","id":791931,"title":"","content":"I'm a huge fan of both HtR and HtV. Comparing them isn't as helpful as it seems because they're really very different games. In the context of Vigil the hunters presented in Reckoning are always going to be playing somewhere between tier 1 and tier 2 in terms of scope, with the one addition of a fairly hefty Endowment.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what you mean by the Heralds being a Deus ex Machina. I'll grant you that there always felt like a lot of overlap between Innocents and Redeemers, and that making Conviction simultaneously the thing you had to spend to use your Edges and the thing you had to save up to buy more Edges was probably a less than ideal design choice. The power level of Edges is spot on though. You're <i>supposed</i> to feel outclassed. Just powerful enough to play on the same field but nowhere near in the same league. Each time you reach a new plateau of power you discover just how much higher the mountain goes.<br /> <br /> The lack of a well defined folklore niche is also intentional. The Imbued are something new, and that should be frightening. You're on your own and the biggest mystery in this world of darkness you've discovered is exactly what you've become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 12-23-2015, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T06:48:58-08:00","id":792150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod?p=788958#post788958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For more like an organized organized than hunters hunted but more crossover friendly than hunter the reckoning I'd actually recommend the sorcerer books(albeit with heavy house ruling, but in a crossover that's expected.)<br /> <br /> Sorcerer paths work surprisingly well if you play them more toward Geralt of Rivia than Harry potter, especially if you cross them with the other numina available to humans through the different game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reckoning is actually very crossover-friendly. Mechanically, its powers don't list rolls against Traits that only they have. Setting-wise, they're the view of any and/or all other games from another point of view. As a general rule, they're not out to exterminate all monsters; that's the purview of only one Creed, the Waywards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T07:26:15-08:00","id":792165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod?p=792150#post792150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reckoning is actually very crossover-friendly. Mechanically, its powers don't list rolls against Traits that only they have. Setting-wise, they're the view of any and/or all other games from another point of view. As a general rule, they're not out to exterminate all monsters; that's the purview of only one Creed, the Waywards.</div> </div> </div> </div>My meaning is that reckoning hunters don't last vary long against any competent supernatural. As caitiff said, hunters work in a setting where them being under-powered and forced to use their brain to take down monsters is workable. In a crossover however they aren't facing monsters that they can simply outwit, they are facing another person with more power, better combat experience, a larger society backing them up, and a wider range of intel. It's like in dark souls when a noob(the hunter) get's invaded by a combat veteran(vampire/mage/werewolf) thats 36 levels higher than him(easier access to stronger abilities), has better gear(access to fetishes/enchanted items), and a speed hack(celerity/rage/the time sphere).<br /> <br /> Not matter the circumstance Hunters Simply CAN'T win as against any competent member of other party as they've had to deal with far worse far more often. The only things they have a chance against are supernaturals with even less experience than them(which will be hard as said individuals will typically have a mentor/sire/entire pack backing them up as they learn the ropes, a luxury that most reckoning hunters won't have as their relative &quot;Newness&quot; means most other hunters will be just as noobish as they are)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:54:27-08:00","id":792479,"title":"","content":"Note that Hunters in Reckoning don't really exist in a crossover WoD. Their books go out of their way to show you that you might encounter WoD stuff... but you probably won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T15:51:12-08:00","id":793296,"title":"","content":"oh curious... does true faith effect Garou?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T19:20:05-08:00","id":793378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod?p=793296#post793296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious... does true faith effect Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but how it does is different between editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:42:03-08:00","id":793543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod?p=793296#post793296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious... does true faith effect Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I read somewhere that it forces them into homid/disrupts gifts, but I don't remember where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:21:56-08:00","id":793583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod?p=793543#post793543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I read somewhere that it forces them into homid/disrupts gifts, but I don't remember where.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, in past editions, it made Rage more difficult to use, so they could still gut the faithful easily, they just wouldn't be as filled with anger while doing it. As of HH2, they can be kept at bay, and a number of Gifts and such likely fall under the list of powers that various levels of TF no-sells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:24:58-08:00","id":794386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/788708-hunter-the-reckoning-vs-vigil-type-hunters-in-the-owod?p=793583#post793583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, in past editions, it made Rage more difficult to use, so they could still gut the faithful easily, they just wouldn't be as filled with anger while doing it. As of HH2, they can be kept at bay, and a number of Gifts and such likely fall under the list of powers that various levels of TF no-sells.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not exactly sure why and how that rule came into play... Considering that True Faith is not really a thing in Werewolf...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:50:30-08:00","id":797028,"title":"","content":"It's not a thing in <b>Werewolf</b>; but <b>Inquisition</b> expanded the eponymous organization from \u201cwe fight vampires\u201d to \u201cwe fight vampires and other monsters\u201d, including werewolves. Since the Inquisition's primary supernatural weapon is True Faith (no Monty Python references, please), the book addressed how True Faith interacts with all of the supernatural types that were known at the time (I think; it's possible that they overlooked changelings). <br /> <br /> Frankly, I find it to be rather curious that the discussion has turned to True Faith, considering that the <b>Hunter Player's Guide</b> suggested the possibility of reskinning <b>HtR</b>'s mechanics as an alternate system for representing True Faith \u2014 a concept that <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b> ran with. I'm not terribly fond of the \u201clatter days\u201d metaplot (which kicked off with the Year of the Reckoning); but the notion of recasting the Imbued as the Faithful is something I could get behind. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Getting back to the original topic, kind of: I find myself wondering what a <b>Hunter Anniversary Edition</b> would look like. It's been, what, sixteen years since the Reckoning? <b>Hunter: Utopia</b>'s notion of getting people organized <i>can't</i> still be a thing yet to come, and something akin to <b>Vigil</b>'s notion of Compacts and Conspiracies ought to be in a HAE core book. <b>Hunter: First Contact</b> detailed early interactions between the Imbued and the protagonists of the various HH/YotH books; by now, wouldn't the Imbued be frequently found in the ranks of these orgs? Which is not to say that all or even most Imbued would be found there; it would, after all, be an <i>Anniversary Edition</i>, designed in large part to address HtR nostalgia. But an appendix updating the <b>First Contact</b> information to account for nearly two decades worth of changes would not be inappropriate, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T21:50:54-08:00","id":797654,"title":"","content":"If I were doing H20, I would rather see the emergence of Hunters moved up to 2012 or something similar. I've played in recent-ish HtR games where the Reckoning still happened in 2000... and the game loses a lot of spark, because the feeling of being thrust into the unknown without the centuries of mystic knowledge that the other games are built on loses a lot of edge if it's been 16 years since the first Imbued emerged; and somehow nothing has really changed in that time.<br /> <br /> Hunter-net.org could also use a significant technological update.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to make a 500-ish page tome (because lets face it HtR doesn't exactly have that much material as-is) I think using Utopia to have some organization building rules in the H20 book would be good because it's a nice support structure for a common game-arc, and it's a good tool for STs to make up their own thing for those that want to run with the Imbued have been around for 16 years instead.<br /> <br /> It's also the first real chance for a second look at the HtR rules, and there's lots of stuff that could use a second look, some optional dials, and so on (ex: re-examining the automatic Derangements since the hassle of tracking 12+ possible Derangements is simply too much, compared to fewer individual mental issues, but ones that get worse with time; which is also much more how it was presented with the few super-high Virtue NPCs).<br /> <br /> I don't think H20 is a place for shoving the YotH stuff, esp. with a very divided fanbase of people that don't want HtR to get YotH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T12:52:13-08:00","id":800695,"title":"","content":"I loved Reckoning when it first came out. Went back a couple years ago to check it out, and the game had lost some of its luster for me. Meanwhile Vigil is, by far, my favorite CoD game, and the Hunters Hunted and Project Twilight were great!<br /> <br /> So yeah, I think bringing elements of Vigil into the WoD would be cool. Some, like the Lucifuge or those guys that had Lil' Wayne for their splat picture would be pretty easy I bet. I'm a fan of Darkness mixing lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}